{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bayes theorem bayes theorem","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md","fileName":"Bayes Theorem.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bayes Theorem","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Probability Foundations]] · [[Count Models and Empirical Bayes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Foundations","Count Models and Empirical Bayes","bayesianprogramming.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bayes theorem bayes theorem","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md","fileName":"Bayes Theorem.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bayes Theorem","heading":"Bayes Theorem","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Bayes theorem relates two conditional directions through the same joint probability:\n\n$$P(H \\mid E)=\\frac{P(E \\mid H)P(H)}{P(E)}.$$\n\nThe prior $P(H)$ is weighted by how likely the evidence is under the hypothesis, then normalized by the total probability of the evidence. The theorem does not create a model; its result depends on the hypotheses, distributions, and evidence already specified.\n\nThe source's disease-testing example shows why accuracy alone does not determine the probability of disease after a positive result. When prevalence is very low, false positives among the much larger unaffected population can dominate the posterior despite a highly accurate test.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Foundations","Count Models and Empirical Bayes","bayesianprogramming.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bayes theorem bayes theorem","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bayes Theorem.md","fileName":"Bayes Theorem.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bayes Theorem","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[bayesianprogramming.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Probability Foundations","Count Models and Empirical Bayes","bayesianprogramming.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}